WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:01.890
Here's Skynet.

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:06.050
Research, strategy, sizing, and execution,

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:07.990
connected in one workspace.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:09.670
Start with a source.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.930
See how its strategies behave in bull, bear,

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:14.050
and sideways markets.

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:16.830
Now change the sizing.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:19.390
This preset excludes smaller tokens

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:21.990
and increases selected position sizes.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:26.490
The historical replay turns positive.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.610
These are simulated results before trading costs.

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:32.850
Move into the terminal to check balances,

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.590
approve a Phantom swap, or follow automated strategies

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:37.770
and open positions.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.190
Then open a recorded trade.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:43.230
The engine work took 81 milliseconds.

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:48.190
The displayed end-to-end time was 2.4 seconds.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:51.730
You can inspect the stages behind those numbers.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:55.550
That’s Skynet. from the signal to the evidence.
